# PepperChat network configuration -- single source of truth for the drifting IPs.
#
# Copy to network.env and fill in. network.env is gitignored because the values
# are machine- and network-specific, not because they are secret.
# Credentials (GROQ_API_KEY, TABLET_WIFI_*) stay in .env.
#
# PEPPER_IP   Pepper's current address. DHCP, so press her chest button to hear
#             it. If it starts with 169.254 it is NOT valid -- see STARTUP.txt.
# WINDOWS_IP  The Windows laptop's WiFi address. This is what Pepper's tablet
#             connects to for the subtitle page, so it must be the WiFi address,
#             not the WSL NAT gateway. "auto" is resolved by the Windows side
#             only (event_setup.py or fix_subtitle_portproxy.ps1 writes the real
#             value back here); from WSL "auto" is an error.
# WSL_IP      WSL's address. "auto" works from both sides.

PEPPER_IP=
WINDOWS_IP=auto
WSL_IP=auto
SUBTITLE_PORT=8088
